From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Derumier <aderumier@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Let the WM reader's seek read the file while
 flushing.

reinit_stream() sets read_flushing so that the demux thread's reads
return no data, then seeks the demuxer to the new start time. The seek
reads the file too, through the same callback, which returned no data
either: FFmpeg searches an ASF file without index for its key frames
(asf_read_pts), found nothing and the seek failed ("Failed to seek
demuxer, error -1"). The demuxer then stayed at its end, every following
read failed ("A non-NULL packet sent after an EOF") and the movie stopped
(Yu-Gi-Oh! 5D's Duel Terminal 6 plays its mode previews as segments of
one WMV file, IMediaSeeking::SetPositions() for each).

demuxer_cs already keeps the demux thread out while the demuxer seeks:
let the reads through for the seek's duration.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/wm_reader.c b/dlls/winedmo/wm_reader.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/wm_reader.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/wm_reader.c
@@ -107,6 +107,7 @@
     HANDLE demux_thread;
     bool demux_shutdown;
     bool read_flushing;
+    bool read_seeking;        /* reinit_stream's demuxer seek reads the file while flushing */
     unsigned int read_flush_generation;
     bool flushing;
     CRITICAL_SECTION demuxer_cs;  /* serialises winedmo_demuxer_read vs winedmo_demuxer_seek */
@@ -956,7 +957,7 @@
     ULONG ret_size = 0;
     HRESULT hr;
 
-    if (reader->read_flushing || reader->demux_shutdown)
+    if ((reader->read_flushing && !reader->read_seeking) || reader->demux_shutdown)
     {
         *size = 0;
         return STATUS_SUCCESS;
@@ -2389,9 +2390,13 @@
         wm_flush_stream_queue(&reader->streams[i]);
 
     /* Seek demuxer back to start_time.  Hold demuxer_cs so the demux thread
-     * cannot race us with a concurrent winedmo_demuxer_read call. */
+     * cannot race us with a concurrent winedmo_demuxer_read call.  The seek
+     * itself reads the file (an unindexed ASF file is searched for its key
+     * frames), let those reads through. */
     EnterCriticalSection(&reader->demuxer_cs);
+    reader->read_seeking = true;
     winedmo_demuxer_seek(reader->demuxer, reader->start_time);
+    reader->read_seeking = false;
     LeaveCriticalSection(&reader->demuxer_cs);
 
     /* Recreate decoders and reset EOS flags */
-- 
